        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Migrate CookieHeaderCache test overrides to task-local scopes",
        "body": "## Summary\nMigrate `CookieHeaderCache`'s legacyBaseURL and display-interval (staleness / unavailable-retry) test\noverrides off their process-global `nonisolated(unsafe)` statics + NSLocks onto task-local scopes. Part of #2204.\n\n## Changes\n- `legacyBaseURL`: remove the static + its `NSLock` + setter; the reader returns `nil` when the task-local\n  isn't set (the existing `withLegacyBaseURLOverrideForTesting` scope is the sole override path).\n- Display intervals: add `@TaskLocal` stores + `withDisplay…IntervalOverrideForTesting` scopes (new\n  `CookieHeaderCache+TestingOverrides.swift` extension), readers now read `taskLocal ?? default`, and remove\n  the statics + `displayIntervalOverrideLock` + setters.\n- Move the ~32 test call sites to the scoped `with…{ }` form.\n- **Supersedes #2205**: replaces `displayIntervalOverrideLock` with task-local isolation (eliminate-shared-state\n  over locking) and removes the now-obsolete `DisplayIntervalOverrideConcurrencyTests` (an opt-in TSan stress of\n  that lock — the process-global race it exercised no longer exists).\n\n## Validation\n- `make check` → 0 violations / 1465 files.\n- Full suite, contract config (`GROUP_SIZE=4 TIMEOUT=120 RETRY=0`): **659 selections / 165 groups, first-pass\n  165/165, 0 failed, 0 retries, 0 timeouts** (477s). CookieHeaderCache suite: 41/41.\n- Behavior-neutral: overrides were never written outside `…ForTesting` seams; task-local scoping eliminates\n  the race rather than locking it.\n\n## Related\n- Part of https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/issues/2204 · follows #2239, #2240, #2242 · supersedes #2205's display-interval lock.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Remaining #2204 seam (`KeychainAccessGate`) — separate PR. No account/auth-file behavior changes. Screenshots not applicable (non-UI).\n\n## Notes\n- No CHANGELOG entry — internal test synchronization only.\n\nReview history: https://gist.github.com/242872d9d6e48e491208421a709be6ce\nAuthored with Claude.\n",
